<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65705" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείλια</span></b> , τά, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλίσσω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>soothing things</i>, esp. of gifts, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγὼ δ᾽ ἐπὶ μ. δώσω</span>, of a bridal dowry, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.147
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				289
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				2
			</span></i>; so of playthings, etc., <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.146
			</span></i>: sg., ib.<i><span class="en">
				135
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>propitiations</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμοσιν . . νόστῳ ἔπι μ. θέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.1549
				</span></i>
			; of <i>offerings</i> to the dead, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				36.230
			</span></i> (Rhodes, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>): rarely in sg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείλιον ἀπλοΐης</span>
			<i>charm against</i> storms, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				230
			</span></i>; <i>offering</i> to a god, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.75
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>satisfaction, penalty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τείσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.594
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
